\[\begin{vmatrix} a & b+c-a & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{vmatrix}.\]Then we can add together the first and third rows and get \[\begin{vmatrix} a+c & b+c-a & c+a+c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{vmatrix}.\]Finally, subtract the second row from the first: we compute the determinant of 
\[\begin{vmatrix} a+c-b & 0 & 2c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{vmatrix}.\]By Laplace expansion along the second column, we get  \[c \begin{vmatrix}
a+c-b & 2c \\ c & a \\ \end{vmatrix} - a\begin{vmatrix}
a+c-b & c \\ c & b \end{vmatrix} = c((a+c-b)a-2c^2) - a\left( (a+c-b)b-c^2\right).\]Performing the multiplications and adding, we get $abc + a^2c + ac^2 - 2c^3 - ab^2 - ac^2 + ac^2 + bc^2 = abc + a^2c-ac^2 - ab^2-bc^2.$</think> <answer> $\boxed{abc}$ </answer>

