&= \frac{\frac{1}{3x} - x}{1 + \frac{1}{3x} \cdot x} \\
&= \frac{\frac{1-3x^2}{3x}}{\frac{1+3x^2}{3x}} \\
&= \frac{1-3x^2}{3x^2+1}.
\end{align*}Therefore $\angle APB = \tan^{-1} \left(\frac{1-3x^2}{3x^2+1} \right),$ which is maximized at $x = 0.$  Then
\[\frac{1-3(0)^2}{3(0)^2+1} = 1,\]so $\angle APB = \tan^{-1} \left(\frac{1-3x^2}{3x^2+1} \right) = \boxed{45^{\circ}}.$ [/asy]

